category: science

entry electric-force
term: Electric Force
related_terms: proton
related_terms: electron
related_terms: strong-force
related_terms: atom
quick_facts: Like charges push apart and opposite charges pull together
quick_facts: It keeps electrons around the nucleus
quick_facts: It pushes the protons in a nucleus apart
quick_facts: Between particles it is far stronger than gravity
quick_facts: It is also called the Coulomb force

sources:
    {"organization":"OpenStax","title":"University Physics Volume 2: Electric Charge","url":"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-1-electric-charge"}

definition:
    The force between electric charges. Opposite charges pull together and like charges push apart. In an atom it pulls the electrons toward the nucleus. Inside the nucleus it pushes the positive protons away from each other, and the strong force has to hold them together.
